Chapter: CvmmUsbTable
  cites Cvmm chapter UsbLive
  cites Cvmm chapter UsbManager
  cites Works chapter GopUsb
  cites Works chapter GopUsbKbd
  cites Works chapter GopUsbMouse
  cites Works chapter GopUsbMsc
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Booted with -hid-combo (the sidecar): codex-vm presents one xHCI device
 carrying a boot keyboard and a mouse. Before usb-attach walks the bus the
 view is empty; after it, the view shows the host and both HID devices, and
 no disk because none is attached over USB.

Section: Report

  ut-rows : List UsbDevice, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  ut-rows (ds) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else let d = list-at ds i
    in ut-rows ds (i + 1) n (acc & " [" & d.usb-id & " " & usb-class-label (d.usb-class) & " " & usb-speed-label (d.usb-speed) & "]")

  ut-line : Text, UsbManagerState -> Text
  ut-line (tag) (st) = tag & " hosts " & show (st.um-host-controllers) & " devices " & show (st.um-device-count) & ut-rows (st.um-devices) 0 (st.um-device-count) ""

Section: Entry
  opening : [Console, Device.Port] Nothing = act
    let before = um-from-attach (UsbAttach { ua-kbd = kbd-no-kbd, ua-mouse = mouse-no-mouse, ua-disk = msc-no-disk })
    in act
      a <- usb-attach
      print-line-uni (ut-line "before" before)
      print-line-uni (ut-line "after" (um-from-attach a))
    end
  end